tty  = terminal type

hostname = which is machine in work

whoami = user name information

w = daya , users , load , average

ls cpu = list cpu system information

free  = free command

free -h = command is used in Linux to display the total, used, and available memory (RAM and Swap) of the system.

uname =  command is used to display essential system information regarding the operating system, kernel, and hardware architecture

uname -a = command is used to display all available system information in a single output string

cat /etc/os-release = file is a standard configuration file in Linux used to identify the Operating System's distribution details

history = all command in history information show

cal = calender present show

cal -j = command is used to display the calendar in Julian Day format

shutdown = command is the safest way to power off or reboot a Linux system because it notifies all logged-in users and stops all running processes gracefully

shoutdown now = command is used to immediately and safely power off the Linux system

logout = current existing user

rebout = system rebout

date -s = date change   { example - date -s "2026-01-11 23:35:00" }

rm -r = command is used to delete directories and their contents recursively

rm -rvf = command is used to forcefully and recursively delete a directory and all its contents while providing real-time feedback

rm * = all file delete current location

cp source destination =  only file copy

cp -rvf source destination = directory copy

mv source destination = file and directory destination change

mv source(old new file and directory) destination(new file and directory) = is specifically used to rename a file within the same directory





















